476741369856	Now we begin the 8th remedial lesson\non basic Virtuaroid controls!
476741369857	Today I'll explain about missions
416611827714	Missions? Feels like I've heard of them, or maybe not...
476741369859	Missions are game modes played with rules\nthat differ from normal matches
416611827716	Huh, what kind of rules are there?
489626271749	Consecutive Battle, Destruction, EX (Explosion) Code,\nand more--there are all sorts of rules
416611827718	Hmm... sounds kinda complicated
476741369863	It's all right, I'll explain them one at a time.\nFirst, I'll explain the battle-type missions
476741369864	"Death Match" is a rule where no points are awarded\nat all, and the winner is decided by KO alone
416611827721	Whoever beats the other guy wins. Nice and simple
476741369866	However, this rule has a special gimmick\ncalled the Damage Floor
476741369867	Just as the name says, the Damage Floor is a floor\nthat damages you when you step on it!
416611827724	That really is exactly what it says...
489626271757	Simple is best, Touma-sama
489626271758	Be careful not to step on the Damage Floor
476741369871	As a side note, it's not a mission, but there's also a\nspecial rule called "Random Mirror Match"
476741369872	Under this rule, all players fight using the same\nrandomly selected machine
476741369873	Since everyone fights under the same conditions,\nit might be the fairest rule, in a way
476741369874	Finally, about the clear rating criteria
476741369875	On clearing a mission, you're rated in 4 grades,\nC, B, A, S, by time left, health, points, and so on
489626271764	Your rank is also a gauge of your skill, and\na high rating can sometimes earn you bonuses!
416611827733	What kind of bonuses do you get?
489626271766	That's a surprise for after you get them☆
476741369879	Next up, I'll explain Consecutive Battle!
476741369880	Consecutive Battle is a stage-clear style mission
476741369881	Just keep defeating the enemy squads that attack you!\nIt's the perfect mission for Kamijou-chan!
416611827738	I wonder what Komoe-sensei thinks of me...
489626271771	Don't mind it, Touma-sama
476741369884	Consecutive Battle comes in 2 types:\nArcade Battle and Challenge Battle
476741369885	In Arcade Battle, you clear it by fighting your way\nthrough the set stages!
476741369886	Win the majority of 3 rounds per match\nto advance to the next stage
489626271775	By the way, a draw counts as your loss, so be careful!
476741369888	Also, in Arcade Battle you can tune up your VR\nto strengthen it before a match starts
476741369889	Pick whatever you like from the items shown in the list,\nand you'll fight tuned up for that match!
489626271778	Tune-ups carry over between rounds\nand disappear after you clear the stage
489626271779	So choose a new one for each match!
416611827748	The tune-up I pick will probably change with my\nstrategy. I'd better think it over carefully
476741369893	Challenge Battle basically has the same rules\nas Arcade Battle
476741369894	However, every element, like the enemies that appear\nand the stages, is decided at random
476741369895	On top of that, every VR gets a randomly\ndecided tune-up!
489626271784	Unlike Arcade Battle, these random tune-ups are\ngiven to both enemies and allies
416611827753	So you have no idea how things will turn out.\nIt might be the rule closest to real combat
476741369898	Exactly! A truly strong fighter should be able\nto survive any situation!
476741369899	Destruction is the BEST!
416611827756	What's gotten into you all of a sudden, Komoe-sensei...
476741369901	I-It's my favorite mission, so I got carried away...
476741369902	*ahem*... Destruction is a mission where you\ndestroy enemy VRs that appear one after another
476741369903	Points don't matter at all! Just defeat\nthe set number of enemies and you clear it!
476741369904	The thrill of mowing down enemies! And the tension!\nThat's the true joy of Destruction!
476741369905	In other words! Destruction is the BEST!
416611827762	Komoe-sensei... I wonder if she's stressed out...
489626271795	Grown-ups have their own stuff going on, don't they?
489626271796	Oh, by the way, if you can't defeat all the enemies in\ntime or your machine gets destroyed, the mission fails
476741369909	Enemies keep appearing on the field one after another
476741369910	Where they appear is random, so where\nthey'll show up is up to luck!
476741369911	The enemies that appear are divided into several groups,\nand these groups are called WAVEs
476741369912	Wipe out the enemies in one WAVE,\nand the next WAVE's enemies appear!
476741369913	Each WAVE you clear adds to the time limit,\nso make good use of that
489626271802	Keep your damage down and keep destroying enemies\nefficiently. That's the trick to beating Destruction!
476741369915	Next, I'll explain Kill Attack
476741369916	Kill Attack is a mission where you take on\nDestruction endlessly!
416611827773	D-Does that mean the enemies spawn infinitely?
489626271806	Correct, Touma-sama.\nThis is your chance to show your guts!
476741369919	The rule is simple. It's a mission where you compete to\nsee how many enemies you can destroy in the time limit!
476741369920	The basic rules are the same as Destruction, but you\nshould taste a unique tension and sense of achievement
476741369921	Enemies spawn infinitely, but unlike Destruction,\nyour HP doesn't recover
476741369922	The fight continues until your machine is\ndestroyed or time runs out
489626271811	The mission rating is decided by the number of kills!
489626271812	Welcome to the Path of Carnage (Shuradou)! Come on over,\nBerserker! Enjoy battles that make your blood boil!
476741369925	It's finally here.\nNext up, Boss Battle missions!
416611827782	A boss, huh... They're strong, of course, right?
476741369927	Yes indeed. In this mission, you team up with allies to\ndefeat a vicious VR on another level in power and size!
476741369928	Boss VRs are powered up by extending the original\nmachine's abilities: super attack up, fewer downs, etc.
476741369929	Destroy the Boss VR within the time limit\nto clear the mission!
489626271818	No points are awarded at all, so be careful.\nDestroy the boss within the time limit no matter what!
476741369931	By the way, small-fry VRs appear before the boss fight
476741369932	If you wipe out all the small-fry VRs, you can get\na special tune-up!
476741369933	If you don't finish them off, you'll have to fight the\nleftover small fry and the boss at once, so be careful
476741369934	Finally, I'll teach you about Pit-In!
416611827791	Pit-In, like that thing in F1 racing and stuff?
476741369936	That's exactly the image!
476741369937	When you have a partner, like in Network Mode, if even\n1 of you gets destroyed, the match is over, right?
476741369938	That's when Pit-In comes in handy.\nIt lets you recover HP during battle
476741369939	When you Pit-In, your HP recovers to max,\nand all status ailments are cleared too!
416611827796	Ooh! That's service above and beyond!
476741369941	Pit-In areas appear at random during\nco-op play in Network Mode
489626271830	Co-op battles get fierce in the extreme,\nso make good use of Pit-In
476741369943	Sometimes glowing panels appear on the field.\nThese are the pit areas
476741369944	Stay still on one of these panels doing nothing\nfor a while, and you'll enter the Pit-In state
476741369945	You can't control your machine until Pit-In finishes,\nbut you won't take enemy attacks either
476741369946	A pit area you've used goes into cooldown.\nNote that you can't use it for a while!
